    "tactics": "Redcaps charge the most vulnerable target they can reach, stack Bleeding as fast as possible, and stomp downed targets with their boots. A summoner who points a Redcap at an enemy and steps back should not expect precision; they should expect enthusiasm.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Scythe [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 3), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 12 damage (8 + 4 Str) [Slashing]</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 12 damage, DR halved (round up) [Slashing]; target gains 1 Bleeding stack</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 3:</strong> 12 damage, DR halved (round up); target gains 2 Bleeding stacks</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Boot Stomp [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 3), Reach: 5 ft (only against Prone targets)</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 12 damage (8 + 4 Str) [Bludgeoning]</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 12 damage, DR halved (round up); target is Pinned until the Redcap moves away</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Blood Thirst: The Redcap's cap must be soaked in fresh blood or it loses its power. When the Redcap deals a Bleeding stack to any creature, it gains temporary HP equal to 4. Iron Boots: The Redcap's kicks and stomps deal full damage to constructs that would otherwise be immune to bludgeoning.</p>",
